        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(vydra): apply request policy to media generation requests",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users running Vydra media generation would not get their configured provider request policy applied when the generation service is reached through the shared Vydra HTTP path.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe Vydra submit/download flow now builds its HTTP resolver from the configured provider request policy, so custom headers, proxy dispatchers, and private-network policy are carried into the generated media requests. The change stays inside the Vydra shared request setup and does not change model parameters or result parsing.\n\nThis is an AI-assisted contribution prepared for Alix-007.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers and operators can rely on the same request policy they configured for the provider when Vydra generates images or videos, including controlled network routing and required outbound headers.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/vydra/image-generation-provider.test.ts extensions/vydra/video-generation-provider.test.ts`\n- Result: 2 test files passed, 14 tests passed.\n- `git diff --check HEAD^ HEAD --`\n- Result: passed.\n",
